 "rulebook": "USBC Playing Rules 2024-2025 and USBC Equipment Specifications: the lane (60 ft from the foul line to the head pin, 41.5 in wide, gutters, pin deck), the pins (15 in, 3 lb 6 oz, 12 in apart), the ball (at most 8.595 in and 16 lb); the playing rules on a strike, a legal delivery, the foul (Rule 5) and legal and illegal pinfall",
 "deviations": [
  "Equipment (ball): the hand holds the ball by a grip switched on and off, which stands for the finger holes (the ball hangs from the end of the hand); a uniform ball, no weight block; it is released when the grip is switched off.",
  "Equipment (pins): each pin is six stacked cylinders and capsules that follow the official profile, with the official mass, centre of gravity and the profile's moments of inertia.",
  "Lane condition: RoboOlympics' house pattern as friction zones (oil, friction 0.04, for 13.5 m in the middle of the lane and 3 m shorter on the outside boards; a 1.2 m transition; then dry boards, friction 0.2); the values are RoboOlympics' assumptions after Frohlich (2004), not a measured lane.",
  "Pinfall and the pin count: a pin is down when it is tilted more than 20.0 degrees or is off the lane's surface (RoboOlympics' rule: a pin leaning on a wall counts as down); the count is taken 5.0 s after the ball first touches a pin. No pinsetter, no sweep; the pit is 0.1 m deep.",
  "Rule 5: the foul is judged at any time, not only during or after the delivery; a fall also ends the attempt as a failure, as in every task of this benchmark.",
  "One ball: the task is the first ball of a frame."
 ],
 "texts": {
  "sentence": "Bowl a strike: from behind the foul line, deliver the ball that hangs from your right hand down the lane so that all ten pins are knocked down.",
  "rules": "The lane is 1.0541 m wide and runs 18.288 m from the foul line to the head pin's spot, with a gutter 0.235 m wide and 0.047 m deep on each side; behind the foul line the approach, level with the lane, is 4.572 m long. Ten pins (0.381 m tall, 1.53 kg each) stand in the triangle of four rows, 0.3048 m apart, its point towards you. The ball (0.218 m across, 2.72 kg) hangs from your right hand. The lane is oiled (friction 0.04) for the first 13.5 m in its middle, less far on its outside boards, and dry (friction 0.2) beyond. A delivery: you let go of the ball (once: it cannot be gripped again) and it crosses the foul line. It is a foul if any part of you touches the lane, a gutter or anything else on or beyond the foul line, at any time. Pins count only if the ball reaches them on the lane: a ball that touches a gutter before it has touched a pin knocks down nothing. A pin is down when it is tilted more than 20.0 degrees or is no longer on the lane's surface; the pins are counted 5.0 s after the ball first touches one. You succeed with a strike: all ten pins down. You fail on a foul; on a gutter ball; if fewer than ten pins are down at the count; if any part of you touches the ball after the release (your right arm may still brush it during the first 0.2 s); if you fall before the count (your pelvis lower than 0.5 m above the approach, or any part of you other than your feet on the approach or the floor); or after 40 s.",
  "venue": "You stand on the approach facing the pins (+x), your pelvis 0.60 m behind the foul line and 0.30 m to the left of the lane's centre line; your right arm hangs straight down, a little away from the leg, the ball under its hand about 0.07 m to the right of the centre line. The approach and the lane are 0.1 m above the building's floor, which surrounds the approach. The head pin is 18.288 m beyond the foul line on the centre line. The ball is released when the hand's grip is switched off.",
  "difficulty": "A strike needs the ball in the pocket beside the head pin, a few centimetres wide, after 18 m of lane on which it slides on the oil and grips on the dry boards; a 6 lb ball is deflected by the pins more than a heavy one, so it must also arrive fast. Nothing but the release aims it, and the body may not cross the foul line."
 },
